1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,451
At this stage of development, the international airport project had a long record of safe tests.

2
00:00:06,451 --> 00:00:19,606
The local team used a computer screen to view every runway, road, parking area, and service car across the full range of the site, from the control-room door to the nearest street.

3
00:00:19,606 --> 00:00:25,066
As Lin entered, a red statement appeared: GET NEW DATA.

4
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:31,391
It was not the style of warning they had designed, nor did it give the next step.

5
00:00:31,391 --> 00:00:35,066
They had little time to wait.

6
00:00:35,066 --> 00:00:40,816
A group of engineers began to draw the system in the limited space on a wall.

7
00:00:40,816 --> 00:00:47,816
Each column showed one period in the data sequence; each row showed a different condition.

8
00:00:47,816 --> 00:00:58,961
A blue card represented food deliveries, a white card represented a medical drug shipment, and a gold card represented a high-security flight.

9
00:00:58,961 --> 00:01:04,501
A thick string formed the link between each record and the person who approved it.

10
00:01:04,501 --> 00:01:08,091
The visual combination exposed a gap.

11
00:01:08,091 --> 00:01:13,731
A red cross marked the exact link where the sequence broke.

12
00:01:13,731 --> 00:01:21,151
The database could capture a driver's face but also contained a gene field copied from another version.

13
00:01:21,151 --> 00:01:24,796
That field had no useful purpose here.

14
00:01:24,796 --> 00:01:33,761
A negative flag should have blocked it under privacy regulation, yet an old construction template had carried it across.

15
00:01:33,761 --> 00:01:40,141
In contrast, the system failed to record damage on the lip of a fuel tray.

16
00:01:40,141 --> 00:01:45,476
The screen displayed noise instead of a precise measurement.

17
00:01:45,476 --> 00:01:51,606
Outside, workers used tape and a tin seal to protect a cable box.

18
00:01:51,606 --> 00:01:57,761
A hammer lay beside the yard marker, and a warning bell beat against the wind.

19
00:01:57,761 --> 00:02:04,236
No one could press the emergency button until the control-room director confirmed the fault.

20
00:02:04,236 --> 00:02:10,576
Lin removed the copied field, but the remainder of the sequence still needed review.

21
00:02:10,576 --> 00:02:21,931
The force of habit had allowed a technical shortcut to play the role of policy, leaving no safety net when the copied field passed inspection.

22
00:02:21,931 --> 00:02:27,486
The team decided to get independent approval before reopening the runway.

23
00:02:27,486 --> 00:02:37,440
They would block unnecessary personal data, cross-check every card, and give each operator a clear phrase for reporting an error.

24
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:41,600
Thus the delay became evidence rather than embarrassment.

25
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:50,464
The airport remained safe, and the group gained time to rebuild the system without hiding what had happened.
